  "id": "unconscious-learning",
  "term": "unconscious learning",
  "definition": "Unconscious learning is the acquisition of knowledge without awareness of what has been learned. In the source context, it refers to implicit learning shown in performance, where people can pick up patterns or sequences even before that knowledge becomes conscious or explicit.",
